# Canonical Hardware FIDO2 SSH Commit Signers (`susanbdev/dotagent` Ring-0 Trust Anchor)
#
# Format (OpenSSH `allowed_signers` -- ONLY hardware-backed `sk-*` key types are accepted):
#   <principal> namespaces="git" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com <base64_pubkey>
#   <principal> namespaces="git" sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com <base64_pubkey>
#
# Bootstrap One-Liner (run locally with your physical YubiKey inserted, then `git commit -S`):
#   ssh-add -L | grep 'sk-ssh' | awk '{print "owner@susanb.dev namespaces=\"git\" " $1 " " $2}' >> scripts/allowed_hardware_signers
#
# Once populated with >= 1 active `sk-*` key (or when `DOTAGENT_ENFORCE_HW_SIGNERS=1` is set),
# `scripts/verify-pr-authority.sh` fails closed (`exit 2` `RING0_HARDWARE_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED`)
# on every Ring-0 PR unless `HEAD` is cryptographically signed by a listed hardware key.
